				{
					"Title": "Extreme rainfall 100-year flow",
					"Text1": "A 100-year rainfall occurs statistically once every hundred years. The highlighted areas on the models are the areas that are worst hit by extreme rain.\nWhen the municipality plans for new buildings, they take flood risks into account and set requirements for various measures. It could, for example, be about raising the ground level and foundation level when building new houses. But it is at least as important to ensure that large amounts of water have somewhere to go.\nOne of the measures in the municipality works to create submerged surfaces in parks and natural areas. By making submerged areas in suitable places and creating them lower than surrounding buildings or roads, the water can collect there instead of causing flooding in places where it causes damage.",
