				{
					"Title": "Trees",
					"Text1": "Here you can see where there are trees in the city. Trees in urban environments are important for our well-being. They contribute to greenery and improve the polluted air coming from cars and factories. The trees in the city also have a temperature equalizing effect by using solar energy for their growth. At the same time, the foliage provides shade and coolness in cities during hot summer days. When it comes to rainfall, it can reduce the load on the city's sewage system by absorbing large amounts of water. Trees also act as a node in a green network in the city. They favor biological diversity and offer habitat for birds and habitat for a number of plants, mosses, insects and lichens.\nDo you think Norrköping is a green city?",
					"Text2": "",
